# Generated by backend/scripts/vendor-react.mjs (inlined into the bundle at build time)
backend/src/vendor/
# Throwaway probes. These are written to measure one thing against the deployed
# system and deleted after; committing them leaves the repository full of
# one-off scripts nobody can tell from the test suite.
#
# The exception is a probe that is not throwaway: one whose subject cannot be
# reached without a model or a browser, and which is therefore the only evidence
# that half of some behaviour works. Those are force-added and listed here, so
# the list says which probes are load-bearing and every other one stays ignored.
#
# `browser-react.probe.mjs` held this slot and was deleted in b75540a; the note
# describing it as tracked outlived it by some months, which is the argument for
# naming them here rather than in prose.
#
#   framework-confusion.probe.mjs — a Svelte script returning JSX is the one
#   defect deliberately left to a model, because rewriting it means deciding
#   where the conditional ends. `react-bundle.test.mjs` proves the detector
#   fires; nothing but this can show the repair restructures the file instead of
#   deleting the branch, which compiles just as well and loses a screen.
#   score-variance.probe.mjs — how much the score moves when nothing changes.
#   The answer is only comparable if the brief is byte-identical between runs,
#   which makes the brief the artefact and a re-typed copy a different
#   measurement. It is re-run after every change to the rubric.
# Anywhere, not only under test/: the pattern was rooted there and a probe
# written beside package.json walked straight past it into a commit.
backend/**/*.probe.mjs
backend/test/*.probe.mjs
!backend/test/framework-confusion.probe.mjs
!backend/test/score-variance.probe.mjs

# Claude Code's per-machine settings. The name says local: it holds one
# developer's approved commands and their endpoint URLs, and it was tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

